1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:00,380
Hi guys.

2
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:06,590
Let's talk about website analytics and let's practice pronouncing numbers.

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:21,800
We can say this website has 10,000 users per day or this website has 50,000 users per week.

4
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:29,060
This website has 20 pages per minute.

5
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:38,060
The average session duration on this website is 1.35 seconds.

6
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,500
Good.

7
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:45,830
Let's practice describing the change in website analytics.

8
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:53,140
We're going to use phrases like to increase, to decrease or to drop.

9
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:55,590
Let's see some examples.

10
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:04,320
The number of visitors of this website increased by 30,000.

11
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:18,440
The number of page views increased by 15%, or there was a 15% increase in the number of page views.

12
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:24,560
There was an increase in session duration.

13
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:31,040
The bounce rate increased by 25%.

14
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:36,770
The bounce rate decreased by 25%.

15
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:42,470
Or the bounce rate dropped by 25%.

16
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,650
How to pronounce big numbers.

17
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:52,190
This number is pronounced 100,000.

18
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:58,350
135,000.

19
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:01,590
2 million.

20
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:05,360
10 million.

21
00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:10,490
25 million.

22
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:16,160
This website has 2 million users.

23
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:21,350
This page has 10 million views.

24
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:28,040
This app has 35 million downloads.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:37,760
Very good practice pronouncing the numbers and use them to describe your website analytics.

26
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,320
Thank you and see you next time.
